--   The single-bit swap (round six, `topSw_step`)
-- statement:
--   **The single-bit swap** of `Y`'s bit `q` with `X`'s bit `q` (`X` below `Y`).
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.R6IL2CTop`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem IntMul.Kappa.R6.IL2C.topSw_step {Ksw : ℝ} (H : IntMul.Kappa.R6.IL2C.SwOK tab l12 τ Ksw) (hT : TopOK l L q Br) {k : ℕ} (hk : 0 < k)
--       (hYX : l.sY = l.sX * l.QL * k) :
--       RecStep I tab (topSw l12) (fun t => CEnv t l K ρ G n q Br fl) l.M Br
--         (swP 2 (l.sY * 2 ^ q) (l.sX * 2 ^ q)) (Ksw * (((l.M * Br : ℕ) : ℝ) + 1))
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Round six, compact controls (I2C): the top selected bit and the record-step calculus
--
--   * `Tl_xor`: the ideal toggle is `y ⊕ (x ∧ selM n)`; with the top bit `q = ρ + n K` flipped as
--     well (`flipS q`) the composite step is the slot row addition `phi g (Fpp K ρ (n+1) px py)`
--     (`tlflip_phi`).
--   * `flip_pull`, `swflip`: the last-bit table rotation (directly when `X` is above `Y`, between two
--     swaps of single bits otherwise) is the record pull `l.stepP (flipS q)`.
--   * `RecStep`: a program acting on the record array `flR recs M` as `recs ∘ π`, with sequencing,
--     branching and skip.
--   * `CEnv`: the registers of the compact program; `topC_step`: the top-bit code as a `RecStep`.
